    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1416",
      "html": "<p>Breeding is unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1416",
      "html": "<p>Deprá et al. (2022) redescribed the genus Heptapterus as having the following shared features: (1) adipose fin extensively fused with the caudal fin; (2) caudal fin non-bifurcate; (3) dark bars and stripes on the back of the trunk; (4) 5–6 pairs of pleural ribs; (5) elongate body with a head length of 16.1–24.9%; (6) posterior extension of the mouth rim short; (7) premaxillary tooth plate with no or a small posterolateral extension; (8) pelvic-fin insertion posterior to the vertical through the insertion of the dorsal fin and anal-fin insertion posterior to the vertical through the adipose-fin origin; (9) 10–23 anal-fin rays; (10) anal and caudal fins separated; (11) supraorbital pore 6 (s6) fused or closer to each other.</p><p>The SL size given is at odds with Fishbase (which lists 9 cm TL) for the same species, however the size given on this site is verified.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1416",
      "html": "<p>Voyage dans l'Amérique méridionale, pp Pl. 2 (figs. 1-4).</p>"
    }
